  "period_note": "Year-end (31 December 2022) position, SOLO basis, primarily from the bank's own audited Balance Sheet, Profit and Loss Account and the 'Highlights on the overall activities of the bank' annexure in that year's own annual report. Interest income (5,883,296,742) is calculated as net interest income (1,255,646,463, reported) plus interest paid (4,627,650,279, reported); the interest-income row itself is blank/merged in the extracted P&L. This figure is independently confirmed: the FY2023 report's own comparative column for FY2022 reproduces net interest income, interest paid AND (for the first time, legibly) interest income of exactly 5,883,296,742. FY2021 comparative in this report reproduces FY2021's own report exactly for total assets, loans, off-balance sheet and equity; total deposits differ marginally (73,061,632,190 here vs 73,103,763,048 in FY2021's own report, a 0.058% gap) and NAV per share differs (13.02 here vs 13.54 in FY2021's own report, the usual bonus-restatement pattern) and EPS differs (0.66 here vs 0.74 in FY2021's own report, same pattern). Total Capital and CRAR directly reported and reconcile (11,126.53/81,107.97=13.719%=13.72%). Tier-I/Tier-II split specific to Solo not found in extractable text this year (only Consolidated-basis CET1 mentions elsewhere in the report); left as a gap.",
